{"id":"word:hebrew:H3802","type":"word","title":"כָּתֵף","subtitle":"H3802 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"the shoulder (proper, i.e. upper end of the arm; as being the spot where the garments hang); figuratively, side-piece or lateral projection of anything","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to כָּתֵף (H3802) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 67 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"כָּתֵף (kâthêph) means the shoulder (proper, i.e. upper end of the arm; as being the spot where the garments hang); figuratively, side-piece or lateral projection of anything First listed occurrence: 1Chr 15 15."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"כָּתֵף","transliteration":"kâthêph","pronunciation":"kaw-thafe'","strong":"H3802","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3802","partOfSpeech":"n-f","forms":["כֶּ֤תֶף","כֶּ֥תֶף","כֶּ֣תֶף","מִ/כֶּ֨תֶף","כִּתְפֹ֣ת"],"morphs":[["HNcfsc",20],["HNcfsa",9],["HNcfpc",7],["HR/Ncfsc",6],["HNcfpa",4],["HNcfdc/Sp3ms",4],["HTd/Ncfsa",4],["HRd/Ncfsa",3],["HC/Rd/Ncfsa",2],["HR/Ncfsc/Sp3mp",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"the shoulder (proper, i.e. upper end of the arm; as being the spot where the garments hang); figuratively, side-piece or lateral projection of anything","usage":"arm, corner, shoulder(-piece), side, undersetter.","full":"H3802. katheph כָּתֵף noun feminine Exod 27:15 shoulder, shoulder-blade, side (Late Hebrew id. ; Aramaic כַּתְמָּא , Arabic ); — absolute ׳כ Zech 7:11 +; construct כֶּתֶף 1Kin 6:8 +, app. כָּתֵף Isa 11:14 (but regard as apposition, or read כֶּתֶף ); suffix כְּתֵפִי Job 31:22 ; כְּתֵפָם 1Chr 15:15 ; plural absolute כְּתֵפֹת Exod 28:7 +, כְּתֵפוֺת 1Kin 7:30 , 34 ; construct כִּתְפֹת Exod 28:12 +, כִּתְפוֺת Ezek 41:2 +; dual suffix כִּתֵפָיו Deut 33:12 3 t., כְּתֵפֶיהָ 1Kin 7:34 ; &#8212; 1. a. of man , shoulder, shoulder-blade (while שְׁכֶם , q. v. = neck and shoulders ), כְּתֵפָיו בֵּין נְחשֶׁת כְּידוֺן 1Sam 17:6 ; compare figurative of ׳י 's dwelling between the shoulders of Benjamin Deut 33:12 (see Dr); תִמּוֺל מִשִּׁכְמָה כְּתֵפִי Job 31:22 my shoulder-blade, from the shoulder let it fall ; as support for burdens Judg 16:3 ; Ezek 12:6-7 , 12 ; Isa 46:7 ; 49:22 (in figurative), Exod 28:12 ; Num 7:9 (both P), 1Chr 15:15 ; 2Chr 35:3 ; compare ׳כָּלכֿ מְרוּטָה Ezek 29:18 every shoulder was rubbed bare (of Nebuchadnezzar's soldiers chafed by armour and toil); as aim of bird of prey Isa 11:14 (figurative); compare shoulder of Moab Ezek 25:9 (figurative, i.e. the side of M. exposed to invasion): 29:7 b read probably כַּף ( ᵐ5 . ᵑ6 Sm Co, compare v a ). b. of beasts , Isa 30:6 (carrying), Ezek 34:21 (thrusting, in figure), ׳כ סֹרָ֑רֶת Zech 7:11 a refractory shoulder (refusing the yoke, figurative), so Neh 9:29 ; of choice meat Ezek 24:4 (|| יָרֵךְ ). c. = shoulder-pieces (always plural) of ephod Exod 28:7 , 12 , 25 , 27 = 39:4 ; 39:7 ; 39:18 ; 39:20 (P). 2. a. slope side , of mountain, יָםכִּֿנֶּרֶת כֶּתֶף Num 34:11 , i.e. the mountain-slopes northeast of the lake, compare Josh 15:8 , 10 , 11 ; 18:12-13 , 16 , 18 , 19 (all P). b. opposite side (s) , that is, of door or entrance, of tabernacle-court Exod 27:14-15 , = 38:14-15 , (all P), of temple 1Kin 6:8 ; 7:39 (3 t. in verse) = 2Chr 4:10 ; 2Kin 11:11 (twice in verse) = 2Chr 23:10 (twice in verse); compare Ezek 40:18 , 40 (twice in verse); 40:41 , 44 (twice in verse); 41:2 , 26 ; 46:19 ; 47:1-2 ,. 3 supports of the bases for the lavers beside the temple 1Kin 7:30 (twice in verse); 7:34 (twice in verse).","rootNote":"from an unused root meaning to clothe ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 15 15","keyReferences":["1Chr 15 15","1Kgs 6 8","1Kgs 7 30","1Kgs 7 30","1Kgs 7 34","1Kgs 7 34","1Kgs 7 39","1Kgs 7 39"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":67,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 15 15","book":"1Chr"